                  <msItem>
                     <title>Beda, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Fol. 230, a waste binding leaf, is in the hand
                        of William of Malmesbury. The leaf was discarded when three columns had been
                        written.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Cambridge, UL, Ii.3.20, Cambridge, CCC, 330,
                        Trinity Coll. 1301, Lambeth Palace 224, Bodleian, Arch. Seld. B.16, Auct.
                        F.3.14, Lincoln Coll., lat. 100, Magdalen Coll., lat. 172, and Oriel Coll.
                        42 also contain writing in a hand identified as that of William of
                        Malmesbury; cf. N.R. Ker in EHR, 59 (1944), pp. 371–76.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="110X/111X">s. xii in</origDate>
